Translation:
(1) One defibrillation after 3 minutes of optimal chest compressions;  
(2) One defibrillation after 3 minutes of standard chest compressions;  
(3) Three minutes of optimal chest compressions after one defibrillation;  
(4) Three minutes of standard chest compressions after one defibrillation.

According to the results of spirometry and the MRC questionnaire, the GOLD staging of the disease is as follows:  
Stage 0 (FEV1/FVC ≥ 70%; cough or sputum production), determined by the response to question 3 of the above MRC questionnaire;  
Stage I (FEV1/FVC < 70%; FEV1 ≥ 80% of predicted value);  
Stage II (FEV1/FVC < 70%; 50% ≤ FEV1 < 80% of predicted value);  
Stage III (FEV1/FVC < 70%; 30% ≤ FEV1 < 50% of predicted value);  
Stage IV (FEV1/FVC < 70%; FEV1 < 30% of predicted value);  
and "Normal" (FEV1/FVC ≥ 70%; no cough or sputum production).
